1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,172
VANISHED SKIES

2
00:00:03,021 --> 00:00:06,982
World War II — three-Minute Cinematic Voice-Over

3
00:00:07,631 --> 00:00:11,160
There was a time when the sky was no longer a symbol of freedom.

4
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:13,532
It became a battlefield.

5
00:00:14,131 --> 00:00:22,940
From nineteen thirty-nine to nineteen forty-five, the world was pulled into a war unlike anything humanity had ever witnessed.

6
00:00:23,589 --> 00:00:26,829
Nations mobilized millions of soldiers.

7
00:00:27,329 --> 00:00:29,225
Cities became targets.

8
00:00:29,725 --> 00:00:33,829
And above them all, thousands of aircraft filled the skies.

9
00:00:34,329 --> 00:00:36,609
Bombers crossed oceans.

10
00:00:37,109 --> 00:00:38,981
Fighters hunted them.

11
00:00:39,481 --> 00:00:42,770
And every flight could become a one-way journey.

12
00:00:43,369 --> 00:00:48,097
At the beginning of the war, aviation was still evolving rapidly.

13
00:00:48,747 --> 00:00:51,939
Wooden aircraft had given way to metal machines.

14
00:00:52,439 --> 00:00:55,439
Engines became faster and more powerful.

15
00:00:55,939 --> 00:00:59,468
Radar transformed the way battles were fought.

16
00:00:59,968 --> 00:01:02,920
But technology came at a terrible price.

17
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:06,900
Over Britain, the sky became a deadly arena.

18
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:12,152
German bombers crossed the English Channel while British fighters rose to meet them.

19
00:01:12,602 --> 00:01:19,585
Pilots fought at incredible speeds, often seeing the enemy for only seconds before opening fire.

20
00:01:19,986 --> 00:01:24,810
Below them, civilians watched the battles unfold above their homes.

21
00:01:25,459 --> 00:01:28,004
Searchlights cut through the darkness.

22
00:01:28,754 --> 00:01:31,658
Anti-aircraft guns thundered from the ground.

23
00:01:32,158 --> 00:01:36,022
And sometimes, an aircraft simply disappeared.

24
00:01:36,522 --> 00:01:38,394
No warning.

25
00:01:38,894 --> 00:01:40,766
No survivors.

26
00:01:41,266 --> 00:01:45,418
Only an empty patch of sky where a machine had been moments before.

27
00:01:45,918 --> 00:01:48,438
Then came the larger air campaigns.

28
00:01:48,938 --> 00:01:55,201
Across Europe, massive formations of Allied bombers flew deep into enemy territory.

29
00:01:55,701 --> 00:02:01,341
Hundreds of aircraft could fill the horizon, their engines roaring in formation.

30
00:02:01,841 --> 00:02:04,817
They carried thousands of kilograms of bombs.

31
00:02:05,317 --> 00:02:08,605
But they also carried something far more fragile—

32
00:02:09,105 --> 00:02:10,978
human lives.

33
00:02:11,478 --> 00:02:16,949
Inside every aircraft were young men who knew exactly how dangerous the mission was.

34
00:02:17,449 --> 00:02:19,322
Some would return.

35
00:02:19,822 --> 00:02:21,598
Some would never see home again.

36
00:02:22,098 --> 00:02:27,330
Fighters escorted the bombers, searching the sky for enemy aircraft.

37
00:02:27,830 --> 00:02:32,366
German interceptors attacked from above, below, and from the sides.

38
00:02:32,866 --> 00:02:34,834
The formations broke apart.

39
00:02:35,334 --> 00:02:37,758
Gunfire flashed through the clouds.

40
00:02:38,258 --> 00:02:41,162
Aircraft fell burning toward the earth.

41
00:02:41,662 --> 00:02:44,877
And thousands of stories ended in silence.

42
00:02:45,478 --> 00:02:48,861
Yet the air war was not fought only over Europe.

43
00:02:49,512 --> 00:02:54,888
Across the Pacific, enormous distances separated opposing forces.

44
00:02:55,388 --> 00:03:01,412
Aircraft launched from carriers crossed vast oceans, searching for enemy fleets.

45
00:03:02,012 --> 00:03:09,403
At Midway, in June nineteen forty-two, carrier aircraft helped change the direction of the Pacific War.

46
00:03:10,054 --> 00:03:15,406
In the years that followed, island after island became another battlefield in the sky.

47
00:03:16,056 --> 00:03:22,487
Pilots navigated through storms, darkness, smoke, and uncertainty.

48
00:03:23,237 --> 00:03:26,502
There was no guarantee they would ever find their target.

49
00:03:27,002 --> 00:03:29,210
And no guarantee they would return.

50
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:33,813
By nineteen forty-five, the skies over Europe had changed again.

51
00:03:34,313 --> 00:03:37,361
The Allied air forces had grown enormously.

52
00:03:37,861 --> 00:03:44,342
German aviation struggled under shortages of fuel, aircraft, and experienced pilots.

53
00:03:44,942 --> 00:03:47,557
The war was approaching its final days.

54
00:03:48,157 --> 00:03:50,894
But victory did not erase the losses.

55
00:03:51,443 --> 00:03:54,036
Thousands of aircraft had vanished.

56
00:03:54,786 --> 00:04:00,521
Hundreds of thousands of airmen had been killed, wounded, captured, or listed as missing.

57
00:04:01,021 --> 00:04:02,894
Some wreckage was recovered.

58
00:04:03,394 --> 00:04:05,265
Much of it was never found.

59
00:04:05,765 --> 00:04:07,638
Decades passed.

60
00:04:08,138 --> 00:04:10,705
Forests grew over crash sites.

61
00:04:11,205 --> 00:04:15,430
Oceans swallowed aircraft and buried them beneath the seabed.

62
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:17,802
Names faded from memory.

63
00:04:18,302 --> 00:04:20,173
But the skies remember.

64
00:04:20,673 --> 00:04:23,937
Every aircraft that disappeared carried a crew.

65
00:04:24,437 --> 00:04:26,550
Every crew had a story.

66
00:04:27,050 --> 00:04:30,146
Every story had a home they hoped to return to.

67
00:04:30,646 --> 00:04:36,502
Today, when we look into an empty sky, it is easy to forget what once happened there.

68
00:04:37,002 --> 00:04:41,033
But beneath the clouds, beneath the waves, and beneath the earth—

69
00:04:41,634 --> 00:04:44,442
the remnants of that war still exist.

70
00:04:45,091 --> 00:04:46,963
Twisted metal.

71
00:04:47,463 --> 00:04:49,336
Faded insignias.

72
00:04:49,836 --> 00:04:51,708
Fragments of engines.

73
00:04:52,358 --> 00:04:59,053
And sometimes, the final evidence of a life that vanished without a trace.

74
00:04:59,903 --> 00:05:02,543
The war ended in nineteen forty-five.

75
00:05:03,194 --> 00:05:05,065
But for the missing—

76
00:05:05,565 --> 00:05:08,158
their journey never truly ended.

77
00:05:08,807 --> 00:05:12,024
These are the stories of the aircraft that vanished...

78
00:05:12,774 --> 00:05:15,053
and the skies that never forgot them.
